 "MarketEntry-LLM Advisor ⊣ Market-Entry Compliance Governor, a REAL
 compiled `kotoba-lang/langgraph` StateGraph (`:intake -> :advise ->
 :govern -> :decide -+-> :commit / :request-approval -> :commit /
 :hold`), append-only audit ledger. Seven governor checks, in priority
 order, ALL HARD violations a human approver cannot override:
 spec-basis citation, evidence-checklist completeness, Kuwait
 commercial-registration entity verification (`:requires-kw-entity?`
 / `:has-kw-entity?`, grounded in Article 31 of the General Tenders
 Law, Law No. 49/2016 -- Kuwaiti Commercial Register + CAPT
 supplier/contractor registration), local-content commitment
 shortfall (`:requires-local-content-commitment?` /
 `:national-industry-purchase-percent` /
 `:local-subcontract-percent`, the FLAGSHIP check for this
 jurisdiction, grounded in Article 87 of the same law -- the National-
 Industry and Local-Contractor Preference that requires a FOREIGN
 contractor awarded a Kuwaiti public tender to independently clear
 TWO separate statutory 30% floors, not a single boolean/number check
 like every sibling jurisdiction's flagship), independent engagement-
 fee recompute (base + months x rate), double-draft guard, double-
 submit guard, plus a SOFT confidence-floor/actuation gate.
 `:filing/draft` and `:filing/submit` (real CAPT portal actuation)
 never auto-commit in any phase; `interrupt-before
 #{:request-approval}` pauses escalated requests for real human
 sign-off via a checkpointer, and BOTH `:commit` and `:hold` durably
 append to the real audit ledger (`store/append-ledger!`). Store has
 a `MemStore` and a `DatomicStore` (via `kotoba-lang/langchain-store`,
 no hand-rolled EDN-blob codec), proven equivalent by a shared
 store-contract test. `statute.facts` additionally carries 6 Kuwait
 laws (General Tenders Law No. 49/2016, Commercial Companies Law No.
 1/2016, Direct Investment Promotion Law No. 116/2013, Kuwaiti Income
 Tax Decree No. 3/1955, Tax Law on Multinational Enterprise Groups
 Decree-Law No. 157/2024, Private Sector Labour Law No. 6/2010)
 confirmed this session against capt.gov.kw / kdipa.gov.kw /
 mof.gov.kw / manpower.gov.kw -- several via the Internet Archive
 Wayback Machine where the live site returned a genuine Cloudflare
 bot-detection challenge (capt.gov.kw) or otherwise failed to connect
 (kdipa.gov.kw 503, mof.gov.kw / manpower.gov.kw timeout); the live
 challenge was never bypassed."}
